	(text "right key board, generated by tools/sch_keys.py from layout/keys.json (52 switches, 52 LEDs). Diode anode to the switch (column side), cathode on the row net. LED rail +5V_LED is switched by the TPS22918 (expander LED_EN, 100k pull-down).\nLED_CT 1n: about 2.5 ms rise, inrush about 0.2 A into the rail's bulk. 220 R in front of the first LED (DIN must not exceed the LED rail by 0.5 V when the rail is off).\nMatrix diodes are Schottky: a 1N4148 at 0.3 mA leaves the column above the expander's 0.2 VDD input-low limit. INTA of every chip is wired to INT (firmware sets open drain before enabling interrupts; pull-up on the port board); INTB unused.\nJ_DIAL pin-out matches hardware/dial J901: 1 ROW, 2 DIAL_A, 3 GND, 4 DIAL_B, 5 COL (the dial push key is a matrix key on the dial board)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 528.32 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			) (justify left top)
		)
